  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1:
A police presence is operating in and around each FMS capital and at least one other urban area in each FMS.
2:
% of SPF and FMS Police registering significant improvement in the functional areas (HR, finance, asset and data management). % contribution from JPP  towards more effective strategic direction in policing services, including support to development of legislation and policy. 
3:
% of operations and activities conducted jointly between the Federal and FMS police. No of Police Plans (SFP and FMS Police) that are revised annually.
4:
% of general population (disaggregated by gender) satisfied with SPF&amp;FMS Police Services. % of individuals satisfied with FMS and SPF engagement with the community.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1: 
JL: 580 state police in Kismayo; 
SW: 440 state police in Baidoa and 30 in Barawe; 
HirS: 56 SPF in Beletweyne and 60 in Jowhar; 
PL: 3,400 state police.
Banadir:  1,195 and 5,031 in SPF HQ.
2:
Public Finance Management used for as a platform for Financial Management. Agreement on NPM, including on structure of police at federal and state levels and on various implementation structures for police 
3: 
Agreement on NPM, including on structure of police at federal and state levels and on various implementation structures for police 
4:
2016 Rule of Law Public perception Survey report. 2017 Annual SPF and FMS Police perception survey</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consolidated 
- Implement Somali Police Training Work Plan 2020
- Complete Police Act consultations
Galmudug
- Conduct a training of trainers and human rights training for 700 police officers, technical support and monitoring
- Community Consultation Workshops on the Galmudug State Police Plan
Hishabelle
- 4 community policing workshops
- 2 community-based assessments
Puntland
- Training of Senior Police Officers, Mid Rank Officers and Station Commanders and Deputies.
- The community-policing model and a crime reduction mechanism are developed and adopted.
- Provide support to institutional development in civilian oversight and governance of policing.
- Support to develop a management capacity of the police Human resource department
Somali Police Force
- complete Leadership development training
- Recruit 2 consultants to develop Somali Police Training Strategy</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of November 2020:
Consolidated: 
- Election security Training of Trainers conducted in all FMS and Mogadishu. Public Order Management trainings complete in 4 locations. Station commander trainings complete in 3 locations. Workshops in Galmudug postponed due to security situation.
- limited progress on Police act consultations in 2021
Galmudug - no progress due to instability
Hirshabelle
- 2 community policing workshops conducted
- 2 community-based assessments conducted
Puntland
- No progress on training of Senior Police Officers, Mid Rank Officers and Station Commanders and Deputies.
- No progress on community policing model
- Puntland Police Basic Recruit curriculum and recruitment guidelines updated
Somali Police Force
- No progress on Leadership training
- 2 consultants recruited and working to consult on and develop the Somali Police Training Strategy</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Puntland:
1. Training of Senior Police Officers, Mid Rank Officers and Station Commanders and Deputies.
2. The community-policing model and a crime reduction mechanism are developed and adopted.
3. Provide support to institutional development in civilian oversight and governance of policing.
4. Support to develop a management capacity of the police Human resource department
Galkayo:
1. Facilitate the peace dialogue and confidence building through implementing the community awareness raising and radio outreach programs.
Galmudug:
1. Conduct a training of trainers and human rights training for 700 police officers, technical support and monitoring
2. Community Consultation Workshops on the Galmudug State Police Plan
Hirshabelle:
1. Community engagement to build police and community trust
Somali Police Force:
1. Leadership Development Training across SPF and FMS</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of November 2020:
Puntland: Letter of Agreement (LoA) developed and awaiting approval from the Minister of Security, Director-General of Ministry of Security &amp; DDR and the Puntland State Police Commissioner. 
Galkayo: Implementing partners contracted and 2 community workshops held
Galmudug: Letter of Agreement (LoA) developed and awaiting approval from the Minister Security of Galmudug
Hishabelle: Awaiting feedback from Hirshabelle Minister of Security regarding the LoA.
Somali Police Force: Leadership training modules developed and under review by stakeholders.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consolidated
- Completion of Federal and State police act consultations
- Completion of outstanding Election Security Trainings
- Completion of capacity needs assessments of police headquarters

Galmudug
- Completion of Basic Recruit Training
- Completion of State police act consultations

Hirshabelle
- Completion of outstanding community policing workshop

Puntland
- Training of Senior Police Officers, Mid Rank Officers and Station Commanders and Deputies.
- The community-policing model and a crime reduction mechanism are developed and adopted.
- Completion of capacity building activities

Somali Police Force
- complete Leadership development training
- Recruit 2 consultants to develop Somali Police Training Strategy</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consolidated
- All planned police act consultations conducted at state and federal level
- 3 outstanding election security workshops conducted
- Police HQ capacity needs assessment conducted

Galmudug
- 200 basic recruit police officers training, training of further 200 expected to be completed in Q1 2023
- No progress in 2022

Hirshabelle
- Remaining community policing workshop conducted in March

Puntland
- Training of 100 senior officers and 200 police station commanders completed
- Community-policing model adopted
- All capacity building activities for Puntland police force completed

Somali Police Force
- Leadership development training of 200 SPF officers completed
- Consultants recruited and draft Police strategy completed and approved by Police Professional Development Board (PPDB)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
